    "created_at": "2025-02-24T11:52:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-24T11:52:57Z",
    "body": "As I see it, there are **two ways** we can move forward to solve these issues:  \n\n## **JavaScript Approach**  \n\n[#9075](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9075) is a great start, but to use it effectively, we’d still need:  \n\n- **`document.topLayer.bringToFront(el)`** → Moves an element to the highest position in the top layer.  \n- **`toplayerchange` event** → Fires when the top layer order changes (addition, removal, or reordering).  \n\nThese additions would allow **dynamic reordering** and event-driven tracking of the top layer.  \n\n---\n\n## **HTML & CSS Approach (No JavaScript Required)**  \n\nIf we want a more **declarative** way to handle this, we could propose:  \n\n- **`top-layer-order` CSS property** → Explicitly set top-layer stacking order (similar to `z-index`).  \n\n---\n\n## **Shared Requirement**  \n\nFor **either approach**, we'd need a change to the current **`inert` behavior** to ensure elements **above modals** in the top layer **do not** become inert.  \n\n---\n\nWould it be best to split these into **three separate issues** (JS API, CSS, and `inert` changes) or combine the JS and non-JS solutions into one? @annevk  \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
