    "created_at": "2026-03-05T16:25:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-05T17:58:39Z",
    "body": "I agree that it's a drag this was closed. \n\nI strongly feel the minimal underlying author need here is to clearly explicate a bespoke ordering via, at minimum, custom named and ordered buckets.\n\nBuilt-in sub-top-layer groups like `low`, `normal`, and `high`, is better and maybe sufficient for some, but I strongly suspect what people making complex stuff need is a bespoke stack of activity-oriented top-layer-like buckets like `tip-info`,`crash-modal`,`debug`, `user-action`,`tool-modal`,`tool-info`,`activity-modal`,`activity-info`, etc. where each bucket displays above the previous, where `*-info` contents are never modal, `*-modal` is always modal with respect to anything lower, etc. \n\nNo sorting system will be sufficient for everyone and I don't see how any sorting system won't be worked around to produce a bespoke sorting. The only question in my mind is whether there's native mechanisms to express the desired sorting clearly.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
